# GCPS-R Pain Scale — Windsurf Rules

## Project Overview
Single-page bilingual (EN/Hebrew) GCPS-R chronic pain questionnaire.
Stack: React 19 + Vite 8 + Tailwind CSS v3 + framer-motion + lucide-react.

## Repository Layout
- All source lives in `app/src/` — do NOT create source files outside this directory.
- `app/src/App.jsx` — single component containing all UI and business logic.
- `app/src/translations.js` — all EN/Hebrew strings; flat object with `en` and `he` top-level keys.
- `app/src/index.css` — global styles: glassmorphism, custom range slider, Tailwind base.
- `app/src/main.jsx` — React entrypoint, renders `<App />`.
- `app/dist/` — build output, **never commit**, listed in both `.gitignore` files.

## Commands (always run from `app/`)
- `npm run dev` — start Vite dev server (HMR).
- `npm run build` — production build to `app/dist/`.
- `npm run lint` — ESLint flat config (`eslint.config.js`). Run after every significant edit.
- `npm run preview` — serve production build locally.

## Language & Localisation
- Default language is **Hebrew** (`useState('he')`). Never change this default.
- RTL is handled via the `dir` attribute on the root `<div>`. Do NOT add CSS-in-JS or direction hacks.
- Every user-facing string must be added to **both** `en` and `he` keys in `translations.js`.
- Use `t = translations[lang]` for all string lookups inside `App.jsx`.

## Scoring Logic (do not alter without explicit instruction)
- PEG Total = Q3 + Q4 + Q5.
- PEG Average = PEG Total / 3 (displayed to 1 decimal place).
- GCPS-R Grade: 0 = not chronic, 1 = low impact, 2 = high impact (PEG ≥ 12), 3 = very high impact (high-frequency + high-interference). See `App.jsx:89-111`.
- Chronicity threshold: Q1 index ≥ 2 ("Most days" or "Every day").
- High impact threshold: chronic AND Q2 index ≥ 2.

## UI / Interaction Conventions
- Slider range: 0–10 for Q3, Q4, Q5.
- Auto-scroll to next question after **3-second delay** on desktop only.
- **No auto-scroll on mobile** (`window.innerWidth < 768`). Preserve this check in every scroll handler.
- Button-based questions (Q1, Q2) scroll to next question after 400 ms.
- `cn()` helper = `twMerge(clsx(...))`. Always use `cn()` for conditional Tailwind class merging; never use raw `clsx` alone.
- Animations use `framer-motion` (`motion`, `AnimatePresence`). Keep motion consistent with existing variants.
- Icons come from `lucide-react`. Do not add a second icon library.

## Email / Results
- Results are emailed via a `mailto:` link to `jshames@gmail.com`.
- Do not replace this with a backend API call unless explicitly asked.

## Styling Rules
- Tailwind CSS v3 only — do not upgrade to v4 or add PostCSS plugins not already present.
- Custom CSS goes in `index.css`, not in component files.
- Do not introduce CSS Modules, styled-components, or Emotion.

## TypeScript / Types
- This project is plain JavaScript (`.jsx`). Do not convert files to `.tsx` or add `tsconfig.json`.
- Do not add PropTypes unless explicitly requested.

## Dependencies
- Before adding any new package, confirm it is not already available via an existing dependency.
- Keep the bundle lean — this is a single-page clinical tool, not a full application.
- Never add a backend, database, or server-side framework.

## Deployment
- `deploy.bat` at repo root: builds from `app/`, then deploys to Google Cloud Run.
  - Region: `me-west1`, service: `gcps-pain-scale`, project: `gen-lang-client-0026629090`.
- Docker image: `nginx:alpine` serving `app/dist/`.
- `default.conf.template` handles `$PORT` substitution via `envsubst`; cache headers are intentionally disabled for JS/CSS assets.
- Do not modify `Dockerfile` or `default.conf.template` unless explicitly asked.

## Code Quality
- Run `npm run lint` before declaring any task complete.
- Keep functions focused; if adding logic to `App.jsx` exceeds ~25 lines, extract a helper.
- Do not leave `console.log` statements in committed code.
- No `any`-equivalent patterns (avoid dynamic property access without justification).
